Call the point where the the runner touches the wall $C$.  Reflect $B$ across the wall to $B'$.  Since $CB=CB'$, minimizing $AC+CB$ is equivalent to minimizing $AC+CB'$.  The wall is between $A$ and $B'$, so we may choose $C$ on line segment $AB'$.  This choice minimizes $AC+CB'$, because the shortest distance between two points is a straight line. By the Pythagorean theorem, $AB'=\sqrt{1200^2+(300+500)^2}=400\sqrt{13}$ meters, which to the nearest meter is $\boxed{1442}$ meters.

